# Monitor: DCGM / NVML integration

- **Round 2 (2026-11-05) — DCGM is a GPU fallback only.** Embedded DCGM ran five fixed-rate timer loops (libdcgm 200 Hz `/dev/kmsg` watcher + two 100 Hz loops, sysmon two 100 Hz loops; ~615 wakeups/s) whatever the watch cadence; MANUAL mode kept them all (405 vs 408/s). Per hour that is ≈ 8 core-s under the `performance` governor and ≈ 109 under `ondemand` (idle cores at 81 MHz). So:
  - **Grace CPU (`host_cpu_hw`, `arm` backend) never touches DCGM:** util from `/proc/stat` jiffies, clock from cpufreq `scaling_cur_freq` (never `cpuinfo_cur_freq`: bogus CPPC values), nominal chain fallback.
  - **Socket power is `host_power_socket`** (`arm_power_hwmon.c` / `arm_power_socket.c`): ACPI `<Name> Power Socket <N>` meters, `power1_average` µW, one row per socket (`cpu_power_w`, `socket_power_w` = Grace meter, `sysio_power_w`, `module_power_w` = GH200 Module meter). DCGM 1130–1133 read **0 / NO_DATA** for every Grace meter on GB200 even embedded as root. `Grace Power` is never module power.
  - **Retired keys:** `dcgm_cpu_power_util_w`, `dcgm_cpu_power_limit_w` (`host_cpu_hw`), `module_power_usage`, `sysio_power_usage` (`nvidia_gpu`); DCGM fields 1132/1133 left every watch profile and the `basic-no-board-power` profile went with them.
  - **`nvidia_gpu` source:** NVML + GPM (`nvidia_gpu_nvml.c`, vendored `third_party/nvidia-nvml/nvml.h` from CUDA 13.2, `dlopen` `libnvidia-ml.so.1`, override `HPCPERFSTATS_NVML_LIB` through `dyn_lib_path_allowed()`) when NVML loads and **every** GPU reports GPM support; otherwise the DCGM path. A GPM sample/metrics failure mid-run drops NVML for the process (one warn) and the next collect uses DCGM. NVML+GPM runs no background threads (0 wakeups/s on GB200).
  - **Converters (verified under dcgmproftester load on GB200):** GPM percent × 0.01 = DCGM ratio (IMMA by convention); GPM PCIe/NvLink MiB/s × 1048576 = DCGM PROF bytes/s; power mW → W; FB bytes → MiB. Pure functions in `nvidia_gpu_nvml_convert.c`, unit-tested.
  - **GPM window = collect interval:** `prepare` (st_begin) takes the first sample per GPU; each collect takes one sample and calls `nvmlGpmMetricsGet(prev, cur)`. A gap < 150 ms keeps the old sample (PROF fields 0 that tick). `dev` = NVML index (equals DCGM GPU id order on GB200 and GH200) and `g_nvidia_gpu_runtime_ndev` is set on the NVML path for shared-node GPU rows.
  - **DCGM is loaded at runtime on every arch** (`MONITOR_GPU_DCGM_DLOPEN`, `dcgm_gpu_dyn.c`); no link-time `-ldcgm`, no build-time `lspci` GPU autodetect. One RPM runs on Grace-only nodes without DCGM.

- **Scope**: DCGM is optional and gated at **configure** time. Do not assume DCGM headers or libraries exist in minimal builds; guard with **`#ifdef`** / build-time flags consistent with **`configure.ac`**.
- **dlopen on every arch** (`MONITOR_GPU_DCGM_DLOPEN`): `nvidia_gpu` compiles against vendored `third_party/nvidia-dcgm` headers only; **`libdcgm` is `dlopen`'d at runtime** in `dcgm_gpu_dyn.c` when the DCGM path's `nvidia_gpu_runtime_prepare()` runs. The binary must **not** list `libdcgm` or `libnvidia-ml` in `NEEDED`. Override soname search with **`HPCPERFSTATS_DCGM_LIB`** / **`HPCPERFSTATS_NVML_LIB`**. On aarch64 overlay builds (`MONITOR_CPU_LIKWID_OVERLAY`) the `arm` backend **always publishes util×freq** `cpu_clock_est_cycles`/`aperf`/`mperf` as fail-soft; LIKWID overwrites those three only when measured cycles &gt; 0 — see **`monitor-likwid-overlay.mdc`**.
  - **Routing**: GPU-path sources include `dcgm_gpu_api.h`, which maps `dcgmInit` et al. to `dcgm_gpu_dyn_*` wrappers.
- **Sessions and handles**: Use **`monitor_dcgm_session_acquire` / `monitor_dcgm_session_release`** in [`dcgm_session.c`](../src/dcgm_session.c) (refcounted; `nvidia_gpu`'s DCGM path is the only user since round 2). Only the **last** release may `dcgmStopEmbedded` / `dcgmDisconnect` and `dcgmShutdown`. Do **not** call process-global `dcgmShutdown` from one consumer while the other still holds a handle (causes NVRM `free_os_event` races and re-triggers libdcgm inventory). Avoid leaking handles across **SIGHUP** reload; release then re-acquire per existing prepare/teardown paths. The dlopen handle (x86) stays loaded for process lifetime; session release tears down the DCGM session, not the shared library.
- **`libdcgm` may exec `lshw -json`**: NVIDIA DCGM probes board/GPU serials via `lshw`. On fleets with **empty-cage mlx Ethernet** (e.g. Horizon `enP6s3f1np1`), real `lshw` triggers **`mlx5_query_module_id` / `query_mcia_reg` dmesg spam**. Ship **`scripts/stubs/lshw`** (installs to `%{_libexecdir}/hpcperfstats/stubs/lshw`). **Enforcement** is systemd **`BindReadOnlyPaths=`** in `hpcperfstats.service` mapping that stub over **`/usr/bin/lshw`** and **`/usr/sbin/lshw`** in the unit mount namespace — `libdcgm` uses absolute `execve` with a minimal env, so **PATH-only stubbing is not acceptable enforcement**. Keep the unit `PATH` stub dir for bare `lshw` callers only. Fallback if binds prevent start: drop-in `InaccessiblePaths=-/usr/bin/lshw -/usr/sbin/lshw` (DCGM soft-fails like `ENOENT`). Do not remove `libdcgm`. Collectors do not need those serials; DCGM soft-fails on empty JSON.
- **Field IDs**: CPU and GPU metrics use **DCGM field IDs** that can differ by DCGM version. When adding metrics, confirm IDs against the **target DCGM version** in release notes; prefer named constants or a small compatibility table if multiple versions are supported. Board-power IDs **1132/1133** are in **no** watch profile (round 2 retired their keys), so DCGM ≤3.1.x (Lonestar6) accepts the preferred profiles; do not reintroduce them. DEBUG verify FAIL `nvidia_gpu`: no rows (expected devices) ⇒ check journal `field group creation failed` / `stage=6` and `Driver/stack probe` `libdcgm=`.
- **Discovery**: GPU index / PCI mapping can change across driver reloads; avoid caching stale **GPU IDs** indefinitely without invalidation on re-init.
- **Fallbacks**: If DCGM is unavailable at runtime (even when compiled in), keep **graceful degradation**: log at appropriate level, skip DCGM rows, and avoid crashing the daemon or blocking the **libev** loop. For `nvidia_gpu` FieldGroupCreate / WatchFields, use the multi-profile ladder in `nvidia_gpu_dcgm_profiles.c` rather than permanently stripping optional IDs from preferred profiles.
- **Grace CPU (historical, before round 2):** the DCGM CPU backend (`MONITOR_CPU_BACKEND_DCGM`, fields 1100–1104/1120/1130/1131, `dcgmUpdateAllFields` soft-reset, per-CPU socket-power painting) is gone; do not reintroduce DCGM on the CPU path.
- **GPU field assign (`nvidia_gpu`)**: Before writing into `dcgm_data_t` / `stats_set`, reject NVIDIA **`DCGM_FP64_IS_BLANK`** and **`DCGM_INT64_IS_BLANK`** families (power, util, throttle/`clocks_event_reasons`, FB, clocks, PROF ratios, PCIe/NvLink bytes). Reuse `dcgm_fp64_value_is_blank` / `dcgm_int64_value_is_blank` via `nvidia_gpu_dcgm_field_*` converters — blank → leave **0**. Do **not** substitute soft-caps or magnitude clamps for blank semantics.
- **Watch cadence** (`dcgm_watch_policy.c`): every `dcgmWatchFields` call takes `updateFreq` / `maxKeepAge` / `maxKeepSamples` from `dcgm_watch_policy_get()` — refresh = the daemon's collect interval (`sample_freq`, set in `monitor_daemon_finalize_runtime_settings` on start and SIGHUP), history = 2 refreshes. Never hard-code 1 s / 3600 s / 3600-sample watches: the daemon reads only `dcgmGetLatestValues` once per sample, and on Horizon c122-018 (sample_freq 60) the 1 s CPU watch cost ~157 core-s/h in the sysmon module. The batch client never sets an interval and keeps each caller's fallback (CPU 1 s, GPU 10 s).
- **Embedded modules**: `monitor_dcgm_try_embedded` deny-lists `DcgmModuleIdNvSwitch` in `dcgmStartEmbeddedV2Params_v1` (no monitor field reads NVSwitch entities; 28 core-s/h on c122-018) and logs which start path ran. The v2 call is version-checked against the runtime's struct size; when it fails the v1 fallback loads every module, so check that journal line before assuming the deny list is active.
- **Util accumulate** (`arm` backend): `cpu_util_*_accum_us` are CPU **microseconds** = util% / 100 × `delta_us` (c122-018 once published 100× `/proc/stat` user time), and must update even when `clock_khz` is missing; gate synthetic cycle/DRAM/FLOP increments on clock only. Util comes only from `/proc/stat` jiffies over the daemon's collect interval; an unreadable tick credits 0 and the next tick reseeds.
- **DCGM 4.7.1 headers** mark `DCGM_FI_DEV_FB_USED` / `DCGM_FI_DEV_MEM_COPY_UTIL` deprecated and alias `POWER_USAGE` to `DCGM_FI_DEV_BOARD_POWER_WATTS`; the DCGM fallback path keeps today's IDs (vendored struct layouts are ABI-compatible with 4.7.1).
- **Monotonic hardware counters**: cumulative readings (replay counters) use schema suffix **`E`** (and width when applicable), not bare gauges. **PCIe/NvLink bytes are rates, not counters:** DCGM PROF 1009–1012 and GPM PCIe/NvLink report bytes/s, so `gpu_pcie_{tx,rx}_bytes` / `gpu_nvlink_{tx,rx}_bytes` (`E,W=64,U=B`) are rate × collect interval integrated per GPU by `nvidia_gpu_link_rate_integrate()` (`nvidia_gpu_estimate.c`, saturating, 0 on the first collect); `gpu_io_link_total_bytes` is the sum of those increments. Publishing the raw rate under an `E` key went backwards on c122-018 (2026-11-09 debug verify: `175 -> 157 decreased`) and broke consumer arc deltas (roofline `_agg_arc_by_dev`). Never delta a rate as if it were a counter.
- **Field count drift**: `NVIDIA_GPU_NFIELDS` (24) must match `g_dcgm_field_ids[]` — `_Static_assert` in `nvidia_gpu_dcgm_profiles.c` when the array changes.
- **Testing**: Prefer unit tests for pure helpers (`nvidia_gpu_link_rate_integrate`, estimate rates); integration with real DCGM may be environment-specific—document requirements in **`tests/README.md`** if new tests need GPUs or DCGM.
